\end{align}
If the altermagnetic term is small, the singlet component is approximately equal to its bulk value $f_{s}e^{-iqy}$, while according Eq. (\ref{eq:tripletfromsinglet}), near the boundary triplets are generated with \begin{align}f_{t}\sim q P^{a}K_{xy}\;.\label{eq:CurrInducedTrriplets}\end{align}


Because both $P_{a}$ and $q_{k}$ are time-reversal odd, this is a time-reversal even quantity.
