This limit does not apply if the PBH increases its mass appreciably as a result of accretion. During the Eddington phase, each black hole doubles its mass on the Salpeter timescale, $t_{\Srm} \approx 4 \times 10^{8}\,\epsilon\,$y~\cite{Salpeter:1964kb}, so one expects the mass to increase by a factor $\exp ( t_{\rm ED} / t_{\Srm})$ if $t_{\rm ED} > t_{\Srm}$ and
